alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The normalization_oracle entry, invoked as `normalization_oracle PATH` with PATH naming NormalizationTest.txt relative to the working directory. Every line of the file that is not empty and does not start with a number sign or an at sign is a test line `c1;c2;c3;c4;c5;`, optionally followed by a comment, whose columns each hold one or more code points of 1 to 6 hexadecimal digits up to 10FFFF separated by spaces. Each test line is one case, which passes when normalize gives toNFC(c1), toNFC(c2) and toNFC(c3) equal to c2, toNFC(c4) and toNFC(c5) equal to c4, toNFD(c1), toNFD(c2) and toNFD(c3) equal to c3, and toNFD(c4) and toNFD(c5) equal to c5. Every Unicode scalar value X that is not the whole c1 of a test line is one more case, which passes when toNFC(X) and toNFD(X) both equal X. Every call appends to an output that already holds the two code points 212B and 0041 for Composed or 212B and 0345 for Decomposed, and passes only when those stay in place, unchanged, followed by the expected result; TooLarge fails the case. It prints up to 10 failing cases, each with its first failing call in the order just listed, NFC before NFD, then the summary line `normalization: C cases, P passed, F failed`, and exits with 0 exactly when every case passes, 1 when a case fails, and 2, with a message on standard error and no summary, when the file cannot be read, a test line cannot be parsed, or the file holds no test line.";
